  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: All three completed experiments share the same encoders (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l) and multiprofile setting, with config_003 (avgpool + weighted) leading at 0.542 acc. We have zero information about whether the RNA encoder choice matters. Question: config_036 swaps scgpt for scvi_n200 while keeping the best-performing image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (avgpool), and fusion (weighted) fixed, isolating the effect of the RNA representation. scvi_n200 is a learned VAE-based encoder that captures nonlinear cell-state structure differently from the generative scgpt model, so it provides a strong, informative contrast. Why this is the best next experiment: With 6 experiments remaining, we must resolve the large uncertainty around RNA encoder choice before committing further budget to the scgpt family. If scvi_n200 matches or beats scgpt, it unlocks a broader, potentially cheaper search space; if it underperforms, it confirms scgpt's value and we can exploit that. Expected cost is similar to config_003 (~2.5–3 GPU hours) since the architecture (avgpool + weighted, ViT-L image) is unchanged and scvi_n200 inference is comparable or slightly cheaper than scgpt."
}

